/* [wxMaxima: comment start ]
Input for the maxima_spawn_count test, which counts how many Maxima
processes one batch run starts. The answer has to be one: opening a file
used to throw away the Maxima that had just been started for the empty
worksheet and spawn a replacement, because Maxima learns which directory
to run in from MAXIMA_INITIAL_FOLDER and reads that only at startup.

What the cell computes does not matter. It only has to make the run do
some real work, so that a wxMaxima which never managed to talk to Maxima
at all fails the test rather than passing it by spawning nothing.
   [wxMaxima: comment end   ] */
/* [wxMaxima: input   start ] */
if 6*7 # 42 then error("The one_maxima_per_file test got a wrong answer.")$
